    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86274" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρεπ-όντως</span></b> , Adv.
		part. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρέπω,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fitly, meetly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				687
			</span></i> (lyr.); <i>gracefully,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				3.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.126
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. dat.,
				<i>in a manner befitting, suitably to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαυτῷ τε καὶ τῇ πατρίδι π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					699d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				835b
			</span></i>: c. gen., <i>in a manner worthy of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῶν πραξάντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mx.</u>
					239c
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
